# One shell command per line, run from the repo root by githooks/pre-push.
# Non-zero exit refuses the push. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# This list is exactly what .github/workflows/ci.yml runs, and that is the whole
# point: a check that fails here fails in CI too, so you learn it in seconds
# rather than after a round trip. Adding a step to one and not the other is the
# defect - a local gate that runs a different graph from CI reports a verdict
# about a build nobody is shipping.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: a syntax check on tools/*.py. `python` and `python3` on
# the owner's machine both resolve to the Windows Store alias stub, which exits
# 126 and would make every line of this list fail identically for a reason that
# has nothing to do with the repo. CI runs on Linux where it would work, so
# adding it there alone is exactly the local/CI divergence the paragraph above
# is about. The tools are dev utilities that ship nothing; when story #11
# exercises photos.py for real, revisit this.
#
# There is no build step. The sites are static files plus the one-line copy in
# the Cloudflare Pages config - see CLAUDE.md.
npm run --silent check
